<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul gives breaks to foreign high-tech investors.</title>
<headline>Seoul gives breaks to foreign high-tech investors.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign companies investing more than $20 million in South Korea's high-technology sector will be given rent-free land from February 1, the finance ministry said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>A ministry statement said foreign direct investment had been hampered by high production costs in South Korea, such as land rental charges, interest rates, wages and transport.</p>
<p>Foreign companies investing more than $100 million in the manufacturing sector would be given a 75 percent reduction in land rental charges, the statement said.</p>
<p>It said the rental breaks would last for up to 20 years.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
